  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33920,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5597,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Tumours often have variable cellularity and a prominent ectatic, branching vasculature.</p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5597.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/thumb_5597.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33927,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5615,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Hypocellular tumours often have a dense hyalinized collagenous stroma. Note the patternless architecture.</p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5615.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/thumb_5615.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33928,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5616,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Cellular tumours may have little intervening stromal collagen, and the vascular network may be obscured by tumour cells.</p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5616.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/thumb_5616.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33929,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5617,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Tumour cells may be spindled or ovoid, as in this example.</p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5617.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/thumb_5617.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33930,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5618,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Tumour cells typically display scant to moderate amounts of indistinct, palely eosinophilic cytoplasm and bland nuclei with fine pale chromatin and inconspicuous nucleoli.</p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5618.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/thumb_5618.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33931,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5619,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Some tumours may have a predominantly collagenous appearance with few cellular areas.</p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5619.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/thumb_5619.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33932,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5620,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Myxoid change is common and may predominate in tumours that have received neoadjuvant radiation. </p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5620.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/thumb_5620.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33933,
    "bookid": 33,
    "chapterId": 37,
    "fileId": 5621,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Solitary fibrous tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Stromal and perivascular hyalinization is common.</p>",
    "source": "Elizabeth G. Demicco",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/37/5621.jpg",
